### URL Structure

Web addresses appear before you begin writing HTML: a URL can point to a page and, sometimes, to a more specific place or search context. In these exercises, read each address as information the browser can use. Start with a Wikipedia article, then examine the settings attached to a search, and finally use a converter to explore how special characters are represented. Try each activity before reading its feedback; the explanations give the complete answers as well as the reasons behind them.

